  "acceptance_criteria": [
    "Define a versioned support matrix covering accepted resources/envelopes, exact base/profile expectations, bundle/reference rules, element and extension handling, terminology policy, and explicit additional-resource decisions.",
    "Provide consistent machine-readable profile and validation artifacts without inventing payer-specific semantics.",
    "Provide deterministic structured validation for JSON/base structure, profile compatibility, bundle/reference integrity, project invariants, unsupported content, and provenance/data-classification gates.",
    "Inventory the unchanged four-file seed corpus with immutable identifiers, observed facts, synthetic classification, and honest provenance/license evidence status; classify it as nonconformant/unsupported under CARIN 2.2.0 and use it only as negative rejection evidence while keeping missing evidence as a benchmark-freeze blocker.",
    "Use only byte-identical, checksum-pinned authoritative CARIN 2.2.0 publication resources with independently evidenced synthetic classification as positive fixtures; record package/member source, license, version, checksums, expected results, and any unavailable required terminology without substitution or invented semantics.",
    "Add only clearly project-authored derived-envelope, negative, boundary, and adversarial fixtures outside dataset/ with parent/recipe lineage and coverage for broken references, unsupported profiles/resources, narrative instructions, and invariant cases; never rewrite the root seed or authoritative resource parents into positives.",
    "Provide a pinned offline validation procedure that proves accepted/rejected/unsupported behavior and verifies dataset/ remains byte-identical without network, cloud, model, production, or live terminology-service access.",
    "Distinguish FHIR conformance from coverage, payment, coding, fraud, clinical, and policy correctness, leaving undeclared semantics unsupported.",
    "Document stable downstream handoffs, deferred decisions, versioning triggers, and required architecture or contract review for later changes."
  ],
  "created_by": "human"
}
